# The play pointer on layouts/hover.jsonc. Nothing is hovered before the first mouse step. A box selects A and B and
# leaves the pointer beside B, on no unit. A hover on C shows C's shield bar, A's and B's bars at the display fade, and
# the crew dots of A and B; a key step leaves it so. A leave keeps the display for the 0.4 s hold, then shows nothing.
# A hover on the Klingon K shows only K's bar. A select click on C hovers C, with its crew dot. A drag outside the
# window hovers nothing. A scroll, and a turn of 0 pixels, leave the pointer at the viewport centre, on B.
# A shot waits 0.7 s after a hover: the display fade passes 0.5, and the display steps one frame after the driver.
# Run it with --layout layouts/hover.jsonc; the layout's header comment has the whole command.
wait 0.5
shot start
box A B
wait 0.7
shot boxed
hover C
wait 0.7
shot hovered
press F11
wait 0.1
shot key
leave
wait 0.2
shot held
wait 0.4
shot left
leave
hover K
wait 0.7
shot enemy
select C
wait 0.7
shot selected
box -20 -20 -10 -10
wait 0.7
shot outside
scroll down
wait 0.7
shot scrolled
leave
wait 0.5
turn 0
wait 0.7
shot turned
dump end
